      <h2>Who We Are</h2>
      <p>KSK Foundation is a registered Non-Governmental Organization headquartered at Plot 24A Hannington Road, Kampala, Uganda. Since its founding in 2011, the Foundation has championed Leadership, Innovation and Enterprise as pillars for community empowerment and poverty eradication.</p>

      <h2>Our Mission</h2>
      <p>To equip young people with practical, real-world skills in leadership, innovation and enterprise &mdash; turning potential into competitive, career-ready talent.</p>

      <h2>Our Approach</h2>
      <p>Each KSK Foundation program pairs structured curriculum with mentorship from working professionals. Cohorts are intentionally kept small and selective, with participants shortlisted through structured interviews and scored assessments so facilitators can give real, individual attention.</p>
      <p>Programs culminate in a practical showcase &mdash; a Hackathon, a project pitch, or a graduation ceremony &mdash; where participants demonstrate what they've built, not just what they've learned.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

